; Undecorated exports a dinput8 client expects. BGE.exe imports only DirectInput8Create;
; the COM entry points are forwarded so that another client loading this DLL still finds
; a complete export table and keeps working.
;
; Scope, stated plainly: the FORWARDING is general, the INJECTION is tuned for BGE. In
; particular, synthetic buffered events are numbered by anchoring to the highest real
; DirectInput sequence number seen (see PadSeqNext in pad_support.h) because there is no
; API to read DirectInput's counter directly. That is correct against every event already
; delivered, but a long burst of injected events with no real input in between can run
; ahead of a real event that arrives afterwards. An application that depends on exact
; cross-device ordering under DISEQUENCE_COMPARE should not assume this DLL is
; transparent. Treat it as a BGE shim that behaves itself, not as a general-purpose
; dinput8 replacement.
LIBRARY dinput8
EXPORTS
    DirectInput8Create
    GetdfDIJoystick
    ; PRIVATE keeps the COM entry points out of the generated import library,
    ; which is what LNK4104 asks for. They are still exported from the DLL.
    DllCanUnloadNow      PRIVATE
    DllGetClassObject    PRIVATE
    DllRegisterServer    PRIVATE
    DllUnregisterServer  PRIVATE
